I finished the draft stage for Tom Rhys Harries and wrote the two requested files in the run folder. Both pass the pipeline's own evidence and draft checks with no blockers. Nothing was published, and no other files were touched.

**The draft (`draft.md`, about 3,350 words, unpublished)**
- **Opening:** the torn ACL he hid on *Clayface*. In his own unscripted podcast words, he hid it "for fear of losing this job." Director James Watkins confirms it came out during the car-hit stunt. His earlier *Entertainment Weekly* line, "shot all of Clayface… hadn't told… anyone," is presented as overstated next to those two later accounts.
- **Type answer:** Type 6 at medium confidence, in 56 words. Type 7 is named as the closest rival and Type 3 as also in play.
- **The case for 6:**
  - Fear as what drives him, from 2015 to 2026.
  - Preparation as "a crutch," and going in without it as "terrifying."
  - Footing in trusted people: the editor who's "got your back," and crediting the team after the No. 1 opening.
  - Motorbikes as an escape because "there's nothing subjective about whether an engine works," which is about certainty rather than novelty.
- **The rivals:**
  - Type 7 gets a full section (curiosity, "reckless" career choice, on-set silliness, the golf banter).
  - The ADHD he has disclosed is treated as confusing both readings, so it isn't counted for either.
  - Type 3 gets its own section (the name-dropping glance, his "relationship" to vanity, worrying how he'd come across "in the press").
  - A closing section covers what the Six read doesn't explain: the tooth-pulling quote he later called a misquoted joke (both sides attributed), the *Parade's End* challenge to the director, and his "wobble" self-correction.
- **Facts handled carefully:** birth year only (1990, Cardiff), and box office as dated studio estimates.

**The evidence file (`evidence-draft.json`)**
- 57 claims, each tied to the exact wording in the draft. I removed four research claims the draft doesn't use (a breath-hold anecdote, interviewers' notes on his calm manner, a teenage gig story, and a girlfriend mention) and kept all 29 sources.
- I added 23 claims so every direct quote in the draft is traceable, using only sources the research stage had already opened.
- The type reasoning no longer refers to the removed calm-manner claim. It cites those two sources directly instead.

One thing to know: the typing is still marked as contested, so this draft goes to the full six-reviewer panel next.
